title: "Collator protocol V4: validator-side segment handling (experimental)"
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Implements handling of V4 segment advertisements in the experimental validator side
    of the collator protocol (`validator_side_experimental`; the legacy validator side
    does not support V4).

    A stored segment is a single fetch entitlement, consumed when a fetch is launched.
    Resolution happens at fetch time: entries are walked oldest-first and the first
    output head that is not already fetched, not in flight, and not known to
    prospective-parachains (including heads that would cycle the fragment chain) is
    requested; a segment whose entries are all blocked is dropped without launching a
    fetch. Because fingerprints are stable across candidate resubmission, this
    deduplicates re-advertised parachain blocks by content. Byte-identical stored
    segments from the same peer are rejected, while re-advertising after the previous
    segment's fetch launched grants a fresh entitlement. V1–V3 advertisement handling
    is unchanged.

    Adds `ProspectiveParachainsMessage::GetKnownOutputHeads`: a batched request
    returning, per para, the output heads of all held candidates plus the best chain's
    parent head hashes, unioned across active leaves. The validator side refreshes this
    snapshot at leaf activation and consults it in the fetch-time walk.
crates:
- name: polkadot-collator-protocol
  bump: minor
- name: polkadot-node-core-prospective-parachains
  bump: minor
- name: polkadot-node-subsystem-types
  bump: major
